## 🤝 Not-for-Profit Organizations Working with Interns

### Data, Policy, & Civic Tech
- **Code for America**  
  _https://www.codeforamerica.org_  
  Civic tech, open government, and data projects; frequent internships and fellowships.

- **DataKind**  
  _https://www.datakind.org_  
  Uses data science for social good—interns and volunteers welcome.

- **Sunlight Foundation**  
  _https://sunlightfoundation.com_  
  Works on government transparency and open data.

- **The Texas Tribune**  
  _https://www.texastribune.org_  
  Data journalism, policy reporting, and internships.

- **Knight Foundation**  
  _https://knightfoundation.org_  
  Supports civic tech, journalism, and data-driven initiatives.

- **Open Knowledge Foundation**  
  _https://okfn.org_  
  Open data, transparency, and open government.

- **TechSoup**  
  _https://www.techsoup.org_  
  Tech for nonprofits, digital inclusion, and data literacy.

- **Civic Hall**  
  _https://civichall.org_  
  Community for civic tech practitioners, including internships and events.

- **American Red Cross (Data/Tech Divisions)**  
  _https://www.redcross.org/about-us/careers.html_  
  Opportunities for data, GIS, and tech interns.

- **Data Science for Social Good (DSSG)**  
  _https://www.dssgfellowship.org_  
  Summer fellowships for students using data to solve real-world problems.

- **Democracy Lab**  
  _https://www.democracylab.org_  
  Connects technologists and nonprofits for civic and social impact projects.

- **United Nations Volunteers (Online Volunteering)**  
  _https://www.onlinevolunteering.org_  
  Many data, research, and analysis projects for nonprofits worldwide.

- **Local United Way Chapters**  
  Often offer data, research, and evaluation internships.

- **Girls Who Code & Black Girls Code**  
  _https://girlswhocode.com_ | _https://www.blackgirlscode.com_  
  Tech, coding, and mentoring opportunities.

